From: Etna Workload <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] authority_missing_double_slash_ac784c3 — serializeAuthority dropped "//" prefix

Hand-crafted re-injection of the bug fixed by upstream commit
ac784c373ef013046ddcb08f73fdc1af0f0272a1 ("Fix resialisation of
authority"). The original bug had `serializeURI` emit `scheme:` then
`serializeAuthority` produce `userinfo<>host<>port` with no leading
"//" — and the `:` was actually `://` in the URI assembly to compensate.

Reversing this patch restores both halves of the bug: `normalizeURI`
emits `scheme://` and `serializeAuthority` produces the bare
authority body, which collapses for relative refs / queries / paths.

---
 src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
--- a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
+++ b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 normalizeURI :: URINormalizationOptions -> URIRef Absolute -> Builder
 normalizeURI o@URINormalizationOptions {..} URI {..} =
-  scheme <> BB.fromString "://" <> normalizeRelativeRef o (Just uriScheme) rr
+  scheme <> BB.fromString ":" <> normalizeRelativeRef o (Just uriScheme) rr
   where
     scheme = bs (sCase (schemeBS uriScheme))
     sCase
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@

 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 serializeAuthority :: URINormalizationOptions -> Maybe Scheme -> Authority -> Builder
-serializeAuthority URINormalizationOptions {..} mScheme Authority {..} = userinfo <> bs host <> port
+serializeAuthority URINormalizationOptions {..} mScheme Authority {..} = BB.fromString "//" <> userinfo <> bs host <> port
   where
     userinfo = maybe mempty serializeUserInfo authorityUserInfo
     host = hCase (hostBS authorityHost)
